BEGIN:VCALENDAR
VERSION:2.0
PRODID:-//Littoralicious//Terroir Cadaqués//EN
X-WR-CALNAME:Cadaqués — eat & drink checklist
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:cadaques-liste-1@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Garotes — The violet sea urchin of the schist rocks\, opened and eaten raw with bread and a spoon.
DESCRIPTION:Say: gah-ROH-tess. The cold-month harvest the whole coast waits for\; out of season\, do not order it. Best: La Sirena\, Carrer des Call — January to March only\; not re-confirmed for 2026\, so call
LOCATION:La Sirena\, Carrer des Call — January to March only\; not re-confirmed for 2026\, so call
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=La+Sirena+Carrer+des+Call+Cadaqu%C3%A9s+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:cadaques-liste-2@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Anxoves de l'Escala — Anchovy cured for months in salt and filleted by hand\, on toast with Empordà oil.
DESCRIPTION:Say: an-SHOH-vess de les-KAH-la. A salting trade the coast traces to the Greeks\; never cooked. Best: Casa Anita\, Carrer Miquel Rosset — the house-salted anchovies\; or the salters' shops in L'Escala
LOCATION:Casa Anita\, Carrer Miquel Rosset — the house-salted anchovies\; or the salters' shops in L'Escala
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Casa+Anita+Cadaqu%C3%A9s+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:cadaques-liste-3@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Suquet de peix — Rockfish and potatoes in a sofregit\, bound at the end with a picada of almonds and saffron.
DESCRIPTION:Say: soo-KET de PESH. The fishermen's pot\; the Empordà and Tarragona both claim it. Best: Es Baluard\, in the sea wall — the monkfish suquet\; phone for the season
LOCATION:Es Baluard\, in the sea wall — the monkfish suquet\; phone for the season
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Es+Baluard+Cadaqu%C3%A9s+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:cadaques-liste-4@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Arròs caldós de llamàntol — Soupy rice with lobster\, cooked to order.
DESCRIPTION:Say: ah-ROSS kal-DOSS de lya-MAN-tol. The rice the village queues for on a small square. Best: Casa Nun\, Plaça des Portitxó — book\, or walk in early
LOCATION:Casa Nun\, Plaça des Portitxó — book\, or walk in early
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Casa+Nun+Cadaqu%C3%A9s+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:cadaques-liste-5@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Fideuà — Short noodles cooked in a wide pan like a paella\, with fish stock and allioli.
DESCRIPTION:Say: fee-deh-WAH. The everyday rice-house plate of the coast\, ordered for the table. Best: S'Estrop\, Plaça del Passeig — facing the beach\; made for two or more
LOCATION:S'Estrop\, Plaça del Passeig — facing the beach\; made for two or more
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=S%27Estrop+Cadaqu%C3%A9s+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:cadaques-liste-6@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Arròs negre — Rice blackened with cuttlefish ink and a dark onion sofregit\, with allioli.
DESCRIPTION:Say: ah-ROSS NEG-ruh. The Empordà's flagship rice. Best: Es Balconet\, Carrer de Sant Antoni — the black paella\, in a room without a view
LOCATION:Es Balconet\, Carrer de Sant Antoni — the black paella\, in a room without a view
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Es+Balconet+Cadaqu%C3%A9s+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:cadaques-liste-7@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Peix de roca a la brasa — The day's rockfish\, grilled whole with oil\, garlic and parsley.
DESCRIPTION:Say: PESH de ROH-ka. Line-caught fish from the slate\; ask the price by weight first. Best: Es Baluard — the grilled fish of the day\, at the window if you booked
LOCATION:Es Baluard — the grilled fish of the day\, at the window if you booked
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Es+Baluard+Cadaqu%C3%A9s+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:cadaques-liste-8@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Ostres a la flama — Oysters flame-grilled and dressed with ponzu.
DESCRIPTION:Say: OSS-truss a la FLAH-ma. The waterline kitchen's signature\, eaten looking back at the white town. Best: Talla\, Riba Pitxot — seasonal\, shuts for the winter (roughly November to March): phone
LOCATION:Talla\, Riba Pitxot — seasonal\, shuts for the winter (roughly November to March): phone
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Talla+Riba+Pitxot+Cadaqu%C3%A9s+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:cadaques-liste-9@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:The sharing menu — Ten plates and desserts to the middle of the table\, from elBulli's three head chefs.
DESCRIPTION:Say: com-par-TEER. elBulli's afterlife\, half an hour from its cove\; about EUR 80 (seen Oct 2026). Best: Compartir\, Riera de Sant Vicenç — book\; days vary through the year
LOCATION:Compartir\, Riera de Sant Vicenç — book\; days vary through the year
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Compartir+Cadaqu%C3%A9s+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:cadaques-liste-10@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Vindaloo at the lighthouse — A hot curry\, served at the easternmost point of mainland Spain.
DESCRIPTION:Say: vin-da-LOO. The strangest table of the cape\, cooking curry there since 1991. Best: Restaurant Cap de Creus\, by the lighthouse — book through its site before driving up
LOCATION:Restaurant Cap de Creus\, by the lighthouse — book through its site before driving up
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Restaurant+Cap+de+Creus+Cadaqu%C3%A9s+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:cadaques-liste-11@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Ous Dalí — Dalí eggs\, the house plate of the bar whose logo he drew.
DESCRIPTION:Say: OHS dah-LEE. Eat a plate under the walls of his memorabilia. Best: L'Hostal\, Passeig — confirm it is still on the menu
LOCATION:L'Hostal\, Passeig — confirm it is still on the menu
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=L%27Hostal+Cadaqu%C3%A9s+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:cadaques-liste-12@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Cremat — Dark rum set alight with sugar\, cinnamon\, lemon peel and coffee beans\, then doused with coffee.
DESCRIPTION:Say: kruh-MAT. The Cuba run's drink\, and the havaneres' glass. Best: Marítim Bar\, on the sand — order it for the table at dusk
LOCATION:Marítim Bar\, on the sand — order it for the table at dusk
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Maritim+Bar+Cadaqu%C3%A9s+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:cadaques-liste-13@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Un negre de l'Empordà — Garnatxa and Carinyena grown on slate\, alone or blended.
DESCRIPTION:Say: NEG-ruh de lem-por-DAH. The red you will be poured all week\; the peninsula grows its own. Best: Can Rafa\, Passeig — the family's Martín Faixó wines with the rice
LOCATION:Can Rafa\, Passeig — the family's Martín Faixó wines with the rice
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Can+Rafa+Cadaqu%C3%A9s+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:cadaques-liste-14@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Garnatxa de l'Empordà — The sweet Garnatxa\, raisined in sun and wind and stopped with spirit.
DESCRIPTION:Say: gar-NAT-sha. The farmhouse dessert wine of the Empordà\; have it with cheese. Best: Mas Estela\, La Selva de Mar — its Estela Dolç\, by appointment\; or ask any table
LOCATION:Mas Estela\, La Selva de Mar — its Estela Dolç\, by appointment\; or ask any table
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Mas+Estela+La+Selva+de+Mar+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:cadaques-liste-15@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Ratafia — Green-walnut and herb liqueur\, sweet and bitter\, drunk cool after lunch.
DESCRIPTION:Say: ra-ta-FEE-a. No two family bottles taste alike. Best: Ask for the house ratafia at the end of any meal in the tables
LOCATION:Ask for the house ratafia at the end of any meal in the tables
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Cadaqu%C3%A9s+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
END:VCALENDAR
